"""Item 7: the pipeline must not read its own output as source.

    python patch_lf_source_library.py --check      # verify targets, write nothing
    python patch_lf_source_library.py              # apply
    python patch_lf_source_library.py --revert     # restore from the .pre_source sidecars

`deli_counter/build/` is the source archetype library AND the directory Deli
Counter writes Level Factory's own missions into, so the output lands beside
the input carrying the same three REQUIRED suffixes and indexes as a building.
Eleven entries there are not source archetypes: nine `lf_`-prefixed composed
outputs and two facades. `lf_lot_demo_001_5017` was drawn into a lot and
measured as an archetype in the 2026-08-09 sweep, and every denominator taken
off this library this week was taken with the pipeline's own output in it.

WHAT THIS CHANGES, and what it does not:

  * `building_library.index` returns THREE lists now -- the arity change is the
    mechanism. Every reader is obliged to say what it does with the third.
  * `building_library.source_exclusion` is the one definition of the rule. The
    two root censuses IMPORT it; they do not restate it.
  * THE THEMED LOT DOES NOT MOVE. Measured: all eleven read `navigable: null`
    with `interior_checked: 0`, so `themed_fitness` already refused every one
    as UNJUDGED and `require_themed_shells` had removed exactly these eleven
    before `index` learned to. The GREYBOX draw does move, and that is the
    defect being fixed.

REFUSES on any target whose bytes are not exactly what this patch was written
against -- a whole-file SHA-256, not an anchor, so a drifted file cannot be
half-patched. Nothing is written unless every target verifies.

Corrects the 2026-08-09 handoff on one point. It said `library_census.py`,
`library_themed_fit.py`, `marker_scope_census.py` and `lot_for` "all pass
through" `building_library.index`. Measured: only `library_themed_fit.py` does.
The other two glob `*.glb` directly, so a fix applied at `index` alone would
have left their counts polluted AND left them disagreeing with the one reader
that was fixed.
"""
